<title>ROMANIA: Romania January current account gap $151 mln.</title>
<headline>Romania January current account gap $151 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's current account posted a $151 million deficit in January, up from $73 million in January 1996, central bank data showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p> ROMANIAN CURRENT A/C	 JANUARY 97	     JANUARY 96</p>
<p> Current account (million USD)  -151		     -73</p>
<p> Trade balance			-135		     -78</p>
<p> Exports (FOB)			 575		     617</p>
<p> Imports (FOB)			 710		     695</p>
<p> Services balance		    -19			 0</p>
<p> Income balance			-26		     -28</p>
<p> Current transfers balance	  29			33</p>
<p>NOTE: Romania's new centrist coalition government has pledged to slash the current account gap to $1.4 billion in 1997 from an estimated $2.3 billion last year.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
